<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<WorkflowBuilder Version="2.9.0"
                 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                 xmlns:rx="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Reactive;assembly=Bonsai.Core"
                 xmlns:scr="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions;assembly=Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions"
                 xmlns:vid="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Video;assembly=OpenRigs.Video"
                 xmlns:orcl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Control;assembly=OpenRigs.Control"
                 xmlns="https://bonsai-rx.org/2018/workflow">
  <Description>A USB camera in no rig.yml, a device piece: Camera-Temporary, such as a calibration's camera on the balance (OpenRigs.Video UsbCamera, the first USB camera that is none of rig.yml's cameras under ConfigRoot), its frames as they come on the BehaviorSubject Camera-Temporary.Data, which the live view streams as a device no rig.yml lists. Its exposure is an experiment parameter the piece declares itself (DeclareDeviceControls, the piece Camera-Temporary): Camera-Temporary.ExposureUs, taken by the open camera at once (OnDeviceParameterSet), starting at ExposureUs and shown at it one second after Start (DeviceParameterDefault). No log and no Ready stage: nothing is recorded from it. At most once in a workflow.</Description>
  <Workflow>
    <Nodes>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ConfigRoot</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
        <PropertyMappings>
          <Property Name="ConfigRoot" />
        </PropertyMappings>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="Value" DisplayName="ExposureUs" Description="The camera's exposure at Start, in microseconds, until the controller sets Camera-Temporary.ExposureUs: the nearest power of two of a second a USB camera allows (15625 is 1/64 s)." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="DoubleProperty">
          <Value>15625</Value>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnDeviceParameterSet">
          <orcl:Name>Camera-Temporary</orcl:Name>
          <orcl:Parameter>ExposureUs</orcl:Parameter>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
        <scr:Expression>Convert.ToDouble(it)</scr:Expression>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Merge" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
        <PropertyMappings>
          <Property Name="ExposureTime" />
        </PropertyMappings>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="vid:UsbCamera">
          <vid:ConfigRoot>UNMAPPED</vid:ConfigRoot>
          <vid:DevicePath />
          <vid:FrameWidth>1920</vid:FrameWidth>
          <vid:FrameHeight>1080</vid:FrameHeight>
          <vid:ExposureTime>NaN</vid:ExposureTime>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject">
        <Name>Camera-Temporary.Data</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Delay">
          <rx:DueTime>PT1S</rx:DueTime>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:DeviceParameterDefault">
          <orcl:Name>Camera-Temporary</orcl:Name>
          <orcl:Parameter>ExposureUs</orcl:Parameter>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:DeclareDeviceControls">
          <orcl:Name>Camera-Temporary</orcl:Name>
          <orcl:Parameters>
            <orcl:Parameter>
              <orcl:Name>ExposureUs</orcl:Name>
              <orcl:Value />
              <orcl:Description>The USB camera's exposure in microseconds, taken by the camera at once, so what it films can be made readable: the nearest power of two of a second a USB camera allows (15625 is 1/64 s).</orcl:Description>
              <orcl:Minimum>100</orcl:Minimum>
              <orcl:Maximum>1000000</orcl:Maximum>
            </orcl:Parameter>
          </orcl:Parameters>
          <orcl:Commands />
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
    </Nodes>
    <Edges>
      <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="1" To="9" Label="Source2" />
      <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="3" To="7" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source2" />
      <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="3" To="11" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
    </Edges>
  </Workflow>
</WorkflowBuilder>
